DEBAZAROS changes to Digilent dvi2rgb 2.0 (vivado-library commit f4613ff,
ip/dvi2rgb/src). The full patched IP is vendored in IP_dvi2rgb/ (that copy is
what hw/build.tcl uses); this patch is the record of what differs and why.

1. TMDS_Clocking.vhd: MMCM CLKOUT1 = 1x pixel clock, serial and pixel clocks
   on BUFG + BUFG (not BUFIO + BUFR): the HDMI_2 input pins are split across
   banks 34 and 35, out of reach of one regional clock.
2. DVI_Constants.vhd: kBlankTimeoutMs 50 -> 2. The alignment sweep waited
   50 ms per IDELAY tap per bitslip (16 s per sweep): hot-plug looked frozen
   (fixed 2026-10-19, ROADMAP.md section 1).
3. dgl_720p_cea.data: EDID ROM advertises 720p60 native + 1080p30 (VIC 34,
   74.25 MHz DTDs); 1080p60 removed (1.485 Gbps is too fast for this silicon).

Apply in a vivado-library clone:  git checkout f4613ff && git apply <this file>
Then IP_dvi2rgb/component.xml also needs new checksums and coreRevision + 1:
  vivado -mode batch -source hw/repackage_ip.tcl -tclargs IP_dvi2rgb

diff --git a/ip/dvi2rgb/src/DVI_Constants.vhd b/ip/dvi2rgb/src/DVI_Constants.vhd
index 83a602e..312d274 100644
--- a/ip/dvi2rgb/src/DVI_Constants.vhd
+++ b/ip/dvi2rgb/src/DVI_Constants.vhd
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ package DVI_Constants is
    constant kCtlTkn3 : std_logic_vector(9 downto 0) := "1010101011";
    
    constant kMinTknCntForBlank : natural := 128; --tB
-   constant kBlankTimeoutMs : natural := 50;
+   constant kBlankTimeoutMs : natural := 2;
 end DVI_Constants;
 
 package body DVI_Constants is 
